// `none` is a reserved keyword. It is the outer absence of the optional type its context expects, written the same
// way as a value and as a pattern.
//
// This directory exists so LanguageTestMatrixTests can name an owning language test for the keyword from the commit
// that reserves it. A program that spells `none` cannot be that test yet: the compiler parses it and then reports
// that it is not supported. That refusal is asserted in Tests/Unit/Golden/NativeOutcomesPending.rux, where an
// expected compile failure is the whole point. Once native optionals are lowered, replace this placeholder with the
// executable case rather than adding a directory.

func Main() -> int {
    return 0;
}
